SUMMARY:Bastille Day French Film Screenings | AFD Ciné Club | July 2026
DESCRIPTION:Bastille Day French Film Screenings | AFD Ciné Club | July 202
 6\nCelebrate Bastille Day with Alliance Française de Delhi through a cura
 ted selection of iconic French films that reflect the richness of French c
 inema—from timeless classics to contemporary masterpieces. Experience st
 ories of ambition\, resilience\, history\, and identity\, while celebratin
 g France's cultural heritage on the big screen.\nVenue: M.L. Bhartia Audit
 orium\, Alliance Française de Delhi\nLanguage: French with English Subtit
 les\nEntry: Free and Open to All\n\n\n\n\nLost Illusions (Illusions Perdue
 s)\n\n16 July 2026 | 6:30 PM\n\nSet in 19th-century France\, Lost Illusion
 s follows Lucien\, a young poet who leaves his provincial hometown for Par
 is in search of fame and success. As he enters the glamorous yet ruthless 
 world of journalism and literature\, he discovers the price of ambition an
 d the illusions behind power\, wealth\, and recognition.\n\nClick here for
  Trailer\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nThe Great Escape (La Grande Vadrouille)\n\n23 J
 uly 2026 | 6:30 PM\n\nOne of France's most beloved comedy classics\, The G
 reat Escape follows two ordinary French civilians who unexpectedly find th
 emselves helping British airmen escape Nazi-occupied Paris during World Wa
 r II. Filled with humor\, adventure\, and unforgettable moments\, the film
  remains a timeless celebration of courage and solidarity.\n\nThe Great Es
 cape\n\nClick here for Trailer\n\n\n\nNous / We\n\n30 July 2026 | 6:30 PM\
 n\nAcclaimed filmmaker Alice Diop presents a poetic documentary that journ
 eys through the communities living along Paris' RER B railway line. Throug
 h intimate encounters with people from diverse backgrounds\, Nous (We) off
 ers a moving portrait of contemporary France\, exploring themes of belongi
 ng\, memory\, and shared humanity.\n\nClick here for Trailer
